The hosted platform layer (issue 5). Everything here compiles only into
the PLATFORM=sdl build; the GBA build never sees these files.

Licensing: shared/video/gpsp_renderer.cc is gameplaySP-derived software,
GPL-2.0-or-later (its header comment carries the full notice, from
SAT-R/sa2 at 393357f7). ext/gbagfx/{lz.c,rl.c} carry YamaArashi's MIT
license (ext/gbagfx/LICENSE). The rest of the layer is this project's
own code after sa2's public shape. The rest of the repository is not
GPL; if the distribution terms of the port ever matter, the renderer is
the piece to account for.

Layout, mirroring sa2-ref/src/platform:
  pret_sdl/sdl2.c       main(), the window, input, the VBlank frame pump
  shared/common.c       the memory arrays and the C interrupt dispatcher
  shared/dma.c          DmaSet/DmaStop/DmaWait and RunDMAs
  shared/save.c         the file-backed EEPROM (step 7): nascar-heat.sav
                        behind the save library's luvdis names, loaded
                        in main(), stored after every program
  shared/input.c        (empty; sa2 kept win32 XInput here)
  shared/video/
    gpsp_renderer.cc    the software PPU
  libagbsyscall.c       C versions of the BIOS calls, after sa2's
                        libagbsyscall/ (ext/gbagfx feeds the uncomps)
  stubs.c               the link-completion stubs; steps 6 (sound mixer)
                        and 7 (saves) replaced theirs, and step 8's
                        fail-closed single-pak path leaves the multiboot
                        ones inert

Headers live in include/platform/.

## Provenance (issue 5)

Vendored from SAT-R/sa2 at commit 393357f7 (sa2 has no LICENSE file):
pret_sdl/sdl2.c, shared/common.c, shared/dma.c, libagbsyscall.c,
shared/audio/m4a_sound_mixer.c, shared/audio/cgb_audio.c and
include/platform/shared/audio/cgb_tables.h — adapted to this ROM's
symbols, structs and headers. shared/video/gpsp_renderer.cc is
gpSP-derived, GPL-2.0-or-later; ext/gbagfx is MIT. Because the renderer
links into the executable, any distributed nascar-heat.sdl binary is a
combined work under GPL-2.0-or-later.
